   $q$The principal made an announcement on Monday that the field trip was canceled. Which sentence says this clearly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"On Monday, the principal announced that the field trip was canceled.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The principal announced that on Monday the field trip was canceled.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"phrase-moved-into-clause"},{"text":"The principal announced that the field trip on Monday was canceled.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"phrase-attached-to-trip"},{"text":"The principal announced that the field trip was canceled on Monday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"squinting-time-phrase"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$On Monday, the principal announced that the field trip was canceled.$q$, $q$Putting "On Monday" at the front ties it to "announced," the action that happened on Monday. When it sits inside or after the "that" clause, it seems to tell when the trip was canceled or when the trip was planned.$q$, 'draft', null)
