   $q$Read the sentence: "The class learned about the bridge collapse from a guest engineer that happened in 1940." Which revision places every part clearly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The class learned about the bridge collapse from a guest engineer, who happened in 1940.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-fix-for-modifier"},{"text":"The class learned from a guest engineer that happened in 1940 about the bridge collapse.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"clause-split-from-noun"},{"text":"The class that happened in 1940 learned about the bridge collapse from a guest engineer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"clause-attached-to-class"},{"text":"From a guest engineer, the class learned about the bridge collapse that happened in 1940.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$From a guest engineer, the class learned about the bridge collapse that happened in 1940.$q$, $q$The clause "that happened in 1940" describes the collapse, so it must come right after "collapse," and moving "From a guest engineer" to the front makes that possible. Changing "that" to "who" with a comma still attaches the clause to the engineer.$q$, 'draft', null)
